            "body": "## Code Review\n\nThis pull request refactors DeepSeek model implementations to consistently use fused projections for the indexer, specifically handling cases where weights are stored in FP8 by dequantizing them to BF16 during loading. It also automatically enables PDL environment variables for Hopper GPUs. Review feedback suggests improving ROCm compatibility by using the is_fp8 helper, addressing potential indexing errors and hardcoded dtypes in the dequantization logic, and adding logging for the automatic environment variable updates.\n\n<details>\n<summary>I am having trouble creating individual review comments. Click here to see my feedback.</summary>\n\n### vllm/model_executor/models/deepseek_v2.py (66-68)\n\n![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nThe `is_fp8` helper should be imported to properly support ROCm platforms where `torch.float8_e4m3fnuz` is used instead of `torch.float8_e4m3fn`.\n\n```python\nfrom vllm.model_executor.layers.quantization.utils.fp8_utils import (\n    is_fp8,\n    per_token_group_quant_fp8,\n)\n```\n\n### vllm/model_executor/models/deepseek_v2.py (750)\n\n![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nHardcoding `torch.float8_e4m3fn` will cause this check to fail on ROCm platforms. Use the `is_fp8` helper which handles both `e4m3fn` and `e4m3fnuz`.\n\n```suggestion\n    is_weight = name.endswith(\".weight\") and is_fp8(tensor)\n```\n\n### vllm/model_executor/models/deepseek_v2.py (764-775)\n\n![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nThe calculation of `block_size` assumes `scale_inv` is at least 2D, which may lead to an `IndexError` if the checkpoint uses per-tensor or per-channel quantization (0D or 1D scales). Additionally, dequantizing to a hardcoded `torch.bfloat16` might cause issues if the model is running in `float16`. It's safer to use the parameter's own dtype.\n\n```python\n    fused_name = f\"{layer_prefix}.wk_weights_proj.weight\"\n    param = params_dict[fused_name]\n\n    if scale_inv.ndim > 0:\n        block_size = weight_fp8.shape[1] // scale_inv.shape[-1]\n        group_shape = GroupShape(block_size, block_size)\n    else:\n        group_shape = GroupShape.PER_TENSOR\n\n    weight_dequant = scaled_dequantize(\n        weight_fp8,\n        scale_inv,\n        group_shape=group_shape,\n        out_dtype=param.dtype,\n    )\n\n    # Load the dequantized weight into shard 0 of the fused buffer.\n    param.weight_loader(param, weight_dequant, 0)\n```\n\n### vllm/platforms/cuda.py (223-226)\n\n![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nAutomatically enabling PDL can have performance implications at large batch sizes. It is recommended to log this change so that users are aware that these environment variables are being set automatically.\n\n```suggestion\n        if cls.has_device_capability(90):\n            for env_var in (\"TRTLLM_ENABLE_PDL\", \"TORCHINDUCTOR_ENABLE_PDL\"):\n                if env_var not in os.environ:\n                    os.environ[env_var] = \"1\"\n                    logger.info(\"Auto-enabling %s for Hopper+ GPUs.\", env_var)\n```\n\n</details>",
